    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d712">

                <pb facs="1113" n="1092" sameAs="frus:frus1948v04/pg1092"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50 Recovery/7–948: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the United States Special
                        Representative in Europe</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at Paris</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-07-09T13:00:00-04:00">July 9, 1948—1 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2539. For Harriman from Marshall. Department’s telegram 2532<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d712-f1"/> inadvertently dispatched without my seeing. While I agree
                    with views <pb facs="1114" n="1093" xml:id="pg1093"/> expressed I have some
                    further comments. Chargé Belgrade had not seen Deptcir June 30<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d712-f2"/> when he spoke with the Yugo official He received it
                    immediately afterward and subsequent message from him (124 to Paris<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d712-f3"/>) indicates that he understands very well position of this
                    Govt concerning western trade with Yugo. We are sure that if further approaches
                    are made Chargé will handle them strictly in accordance with Dept’s June 30
                    circular. We do not feel that Chargé should take initiative in inviting further
                    discussions along these lines at this moment.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d712-f1" n="1" xml:id="d712-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d712-f2" n="2" xml:id="d712-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; it contained the text of the conclusions of Policy Planning Staff
                    paper 35, June 30, 1948, <ref target="#pg1079">p. 1079</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d712-f3" n="3" xml:id="d712-f3-content">
                <p>Same as telegram 849, July 7, from Belgrade, <ref target="#pg1088">p.
                    1088</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
